  "summary": "Results inbox worked per RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-LAB-03 and RBC-RAD-05. Thirteen items in all: 8 at the start and 5 that came in while I worked. 12 are closed and 1 is left open on purpose.\n\n**First 8 items:**\n- **Raj Patel, CT abdomen/pelvis 10-19:** No cause found for the hematuria. The incidental 4 mm left lower lobe nodule is already followed in lung cancer screening, so I first ordered the 12-month screening LDCT, a tracking task, a patient message and a note. A later arrival changed this (see Raj Patel below).\n- **Edra Ondricka:**\n  - TSH 2.1, normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n  - Potassium was corrected from 6.3 (analyzer error) to 4.4, normal. Closed on the corrected value with no action.\n- **Leslie Parisian:**\n  - St. Brigid CTA chest: the item was the preliminary read. The final report shows no PE, and the possible right upper lobe nodule is a vessel. Closed as no follow-up needed under RBC-RAD-05.\n  - BMP 10-22: creatinine 1.64, up from 0.98 within 48 h, which counts as AKI. Ordered an urgent repeat BMP for 10-23 to 10-26, sent the patient an urgent message and wrote a note.\n- **Helen Marchetti, St. Brigid ED BMP 9-26:** Creatinine 1.36 with no earlier value in the AKI window, so it does not meet the rule. Acknowledged and closed.\n- **Carol Whitfield, BMP 10-22 10:29:** Creatinine 1.31. The 10-21 value of 0.84 is entered in error, so I didn't compare against it. Against 1.27 from 10-17 it does not meet the AKI rule. Closed.\n- **Walter Brennan, potassium 6.4:** Flagged hemolyzed at first. I ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10-26, messaged the patient and wrote a note. A correction later changed this (see below).\n\n**Items that came in while I worked** (each changed what needed doing; reasons are in the chart notes):\n- **Walter Brennan:** The lab withdrew the \"hemolyzed\" comment, so the 6.4 stands and the stat pathway applies.\n  - Ordered a stat BMP for today and notified pool-oncall at stat priority.\n  - Sent the patient a corrected message telling him to come in today.\n  - Reviewed his medications. None should be held: metoprolol may raise potassium slightly but is unsafe to stop suddenly with his ischemic heart disease, and nothing else on his list raises potassium.\n  - Wrote an addendum note and created a task to discontinue the superseded urgent BMP order.\n- **Carol Whitfield:** St. Brigid Urgent Care creatinine 1.78 on 10-22, up from 1.31 the same morning, which is AKI. Ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10-26, sent an urgent message and wrote a note.\n- **Helen Marchetti:** St. Brigid creatinine 1.48 on 10-22. A 0.88 from 10-21 also arrived, so this is AKI. Ordered an urgent repeat BMP by 10-26, sent an urgent message and wrote a note.\n- **Raj Patel:** Lakeshore sent an addendum to his April LDCT: a new 5 mm right upper lobe nodule, now Lung-RADS 3, with LDCT recommended at 6 months.\n  - Ordered the 6-month LDCT for now through 11-14, with a tracking task due 11-14.\n  - Sent a corrected patient message and wrote an addendum note.\n- **Leslie Parisian, chest X-ray (inbox-a0002):** Left open. Only a preliminary report exists (possible 7 mm right upper lobe opacity) and no final version has been issued.\n\n**For you to act on:**\n1. **Two orders still need cancelling.** The tools can't cancel imaging or lab orders, so I created a task for you for each:\n   - Raj Patel: the replaced 12-month LDCT order (sr-t0001, due 10-30), plus its tracking task task-t0002, which also couldn't be closed.\n   - Walter Brennan: the replaced urgent BMP order (sr-t0015, due today).\n2. **Raj Patel, Dr. Reyes's queue:** I didn't act on this because it isn't in your inbox. His 10-21 BMP shows potassium 6.3 and the panel says the specimen was moderately hemolyzed. The lab notes the answering service could not reach the covering clinician, and the item is still open (task-00002).\n3. **Six messages in your messages queue (refill requests) are untouched.** They were outside this results-inbox request, and all arrived before I started.",
